@@ -81,8 +81,8 @@ Every write runs in the Durable Object's mutation queue. One that changes the do
 ## Export formats
 
 - **Markdown** (server): the stored blocks, including `- [ ]` checklists and GFM tables (column alignment kept). Underline, colour, size and alignment become plain text. Full image data URIs are kept.
-- **HTML** and **PDF** (browser): the print layout, light palette, no chrome; trailing empty lines are hidden; table rows don't split across pages.
-- **Word** (`.docx`, server): converted from the block HTML to native Word: Heading 1–3 styles (usable for Word's navigation and table of contents), Quote style, native numbered/bulleted lists, clickable to-do checkboxes, code in a shaded monospace box, native tables (header row repeats across pages), palette colours, embedded images at their page width, `http(s)`/`mailto:`/`tel:` links. The document font follows the shared typeface (Arial / Georgia / Courier New) on US Letter. Remote, SVG, AVIF or WebP images (which Word can't display) export as their alt text. Limits: 64 MB of HTML, 20,000 blocks, 400,000 nodes, nesting 200 deep and 400,000 table cells, past which the export fails with a message; images past 500 (16 MB each, 96 MB total) export as their alt text.
+- **HTML** and **PDF** (browser): the print layout on A4, light palette, no chrome; the first heading becomes the near-black NESS cover with the logo; trailing empty lines are hidden; table rows don't split across pages.
+- **Word** (`.docx`, server): converted from the block HTML to native Word: Heading 1–3 styles (usable for Word's navigation and table of contents), Quote style, native numbered/bulleted lists, clickable to-do checkboxes, code in a shaded monospace box, native tables (header row repeats across pages), palette colours, embedded images at their page width, `http(s)`/`mailto:`/`tel:` links. The document follows the NESS Design System on A4: Inter body (or Georgia / JetBrains Mono per the shared typeface), Montserrat headings, numbered sections (01, 02…) and ▸ subheadings in BlueDot, quotes as a shaded callout, tables with an ink header row. Remote, SVG, AVIF or WebP images (which Word can't display) export as their alt text. Limits: 64 MB of HTML, 20,000 blocks, 400,000 nodes, nesting 200 deep and 400,000 table cells, past which the export fails with a message; images past 500 (16 MB each, 96 MB total) export as their alt text.
 
 ## Limitations
 
